# Everything the ocr-runner installs, listed explicitly: requirements.txt is compiled from
# this file with --no-deps and installed with `pip install --no-deps --require-hashes`, so
# only these packages, at these versions, with these hashes, end up in the image. Lock for
# the container target (linux aarch64, CPython 3.13, the python:3.13-slim base of
# qairt-common-base):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --no-deps --python-platform aarch64-manylinux_2_34 \
#       --python-version 3.13 --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
#
# Transitive dependencies deliberately left out: sympy + mpmath (~80 MB, only used by
# onnxruntime's offline tooling) and coloredlogs + humanfriendly (declared by the plugin
# wheel, never imported at runtime).
#
# onnxruntime-qnn is a plugin EP compiled against one onnxruntime release and one QAIRT
# release, and it bundles that QAIRT (~190 MB of libQnn*.so). Pairs, from the release notes
# (https://github.com/onnxruntime/onnxruntime-qnn/releases) and measured on the 21q with
# the EasyOCR recognizer:
#   2.1.1 -> ORT 1.24.4, QAIRT 2.45.41   reads garbage on the HTP (all confidences 0)
#   2.2.0 -> ORT 1.24.4, QAIRT 2.46.0    reads garbage on the HTP
#   2.3.0 -> ORT 1.29.0, QAIRT 2.47.0    misreads digits, detector falls off the NPU
#   2.4.0 -> ORT 1.29.0, QAIRT 2.48.40   correct
#   2.5.0 -> ORT 1.29.0, QAIRT 2.49.40   correct (pinned)
# The base image ships QAIRT 2.45.41 (QNP_VER in containers/base/qairt-common-base), which
# the EP cannot use: too old for its QNN API, and the release built with it misreads. So the
# wheel's own QAIRT is used. To drop it and use the base image's instead, QNP_VER has to move
# to the QAIRT of the pinned wheel (2.49.40): then set EASYOCR_QNN_BACKEND_PATH=/usr/lib/libQnnHtp.so
# in the Dockerfile and delete the wheel's libQnn*.so after pip install (see the Dockerfile),
# and keep the two in lockstep from then on. The line below is read by
# tests/containers/ai/test_ocr_runner_context_binaries.py and compared with the
# `qnn_version` recorded in models/**/*.qnn_ctx.json (and with QNP_VER once the base image's
# QAIRT is the one in use).
# qairt-version: 2.49.40
opencv-python-headless==5.0.0.93
numpy==2.5.3
onnxruntime==1.29.0
onnxruntime-qnn==2.5.0
flatbuffers==25.12.19
protobuf==7.36.1
packaging==26.3
